.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trellis-run 1 "" trellis "Trellis Manual"
.SH NAME
trellis\-run \- Run a task across packages, graph\-parallel by default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtrellis run\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-since\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-with\-dependents\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-target\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-serial\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR] [\fB\-j\fR|\fB\-\-jobs\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fITASK\fR> [\fIPACKAGES\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a task across packages, graph\-parallel by default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-directory\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Run as if started in this directory
.TP
\fB\-\-since\fR \fI<REF>\fR
Only packages owning files changed since this git ref
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR [default: auto]
When to color output. `auto` follows the terminal, `NO_COLOR`, and `CLICOLOR=0`; the other two override that detection
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-dependents\fR
Add the reverse\-dependency closure of the selection
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress normal\-path output; JSON/report payloads and errors still print
.TP
\fB\-\-target\fR \fI<TARGET>\fR
Gleam compile target; `all` runs the task once per target
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
erlang
.IP \(bu 2
javascript
.IP \(bu 2
all
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-strict\fR
Treat warnings as errors (build)
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Trace every command trellis shells out to, on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Check instead of write (format)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-update\-check\fR
Don\*(Aqt check whether a newer trellis release is available

The check is also skipped in CI, when not attached to a terminal, and when `TRELLIS_NO_UPDATE_CHECK` or `DO_NOT_TRACK` is set.
.TP
\fB\-\-serial\fR
Run one package at a time, in dependency order
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-going\fR
Keep scheduling packages after a failure
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR \fI<N>\fR
Maximum concurrent packages (default: CPU count)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the `trellis.run/1` payload instead of the summary table; package output moves to stderr
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fITASK\fR>
Built\-in (build, test, check, format, docs, deps, clean) or a [tools.trellis.tasks] entry
.TP
[\fIPACKAGES\fR]
Packages to run in; all workspace packages when omitted
